WEBVTT

00:02.790 --> 00:04.500
A long, long time ago.

00:04.750 --> 00:07.630
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.590 --> 00:09.930
Nadja, guided by destiny,

00:09.930 --> 00:13.680
is on her way to Italy, and about to cross the Alps.

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
NAAJA

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
Nadja,

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
With your eyes

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
Nadja,

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
NAAJA

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
What do you see?

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
Nani ga mieru

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
The door to the future,

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
Mirai no tobira

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
Sagashite iru

00:34.620 --> 00:41.830
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
It could be so much more fun

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
I will go waving

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
Te wo furinagara

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
But I won't look back

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
Nadja, Your smile

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
Nadja, gives me courage

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Under the blue sky,

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
I will find the place

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
Ashita no yukue

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
where my future lies

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
Mitsukeru kara

02:05.100 --> 02:07.150
﻿Wow! It's beautiful!

02:07.400 --> 02:10.520
﻿It's my first time in seeing something so tall up close!

02:10.900 --> 02:13.190
﻿A lovely sight, and a marvelous height!

02:15.280 --> 02:17.530
﻿It must be taller than Mt. Fuji...

02:18.120 --> 02:18.850
﻿Mt. Fuji?

02:18.930 --> 02:21.410
That's right. In Japan, it's the tallest...

02:21.410 --> 02:22.910
﻿...and, most beautiful mountain!

02:23.080 --> 02:24.340
But...

02:24.790 --> 02:27.290
﻿Will we really be able to cross that mountain with this car?

02:27.290 --> 02:28.500
﻿I'm worried.

02:28.500 --> 02:30.040
﻿Hey now! Kennosuke!

02:30.340 --> 02:32.750
﻿Are you saying that you don't trust my car?!

02:32.920 --> 02:34.970
﻿Crap... he heard me...

02:56.840 --> 03:01.780
A Family in a Storm

03:01.850 --> 03:05.220
Vienna

03:03.160 --> 03:05.290
﻿Nadja is headed for Italy, you say?

03:07.350 --> 03:08.250
I see...

03:08.250 --> 03:09.040
﻿So, my old man...

03:09.630 --> 03:12.340
﻿I mean, Duke Preminger... have you reported it to him?

03:13.130 --> 03:14.340
﻿Yes, that's fine...

03:15.260 --> 03:17.920
﻿Dear, if we don't hurry, we'll be late.

03:17.930 --> 03:18.970
﻿Y-Yes...

03:19.300 --> 03:20.640
﻿We'll talk more later...

03:20.800 --> 03:23.010
﻿So, call me again tomorrow. Bye.

03:24.930 --> 03:26.180
﻿Who may I ask was that?

03:26.600 --> 03:28.640
﻿Forget that. Where's Oscar?

03:28.980 --> 03:31.230
﻿He's already in the car.

03:32.820 --> 03:34.610
﻿Mr. Herman, we're going to be late.

03:34.730 --> 03:36.780
﻿Oscar, call him "Father"...

03:37.260 --> 03:37.970
Yes.

03:38.300 --> 03:39.220
Father.

03:39.700 --> 03:42.570
If you displease Duke Preminger any further...

03:42.580 --> 03:43.700
﻿...won't it become difficult?

03:44.410 --> 03:45.240
﻿Let's hurry.

03:45.240 --> 03:46.240
﻿Cease this impertinence!

03:46.950 --> 03:48.290
﻿You ride in the back.

03:48.810 --> 03:49.310
Yes, sir.

04:04.430 --> 04:06.180
﻿It's a small town, but...

04:06.180 --> 04:07.720
﻿...there sure are a lot of people.

04:07.730 --> 04:09.890
﻿It seems they've been stopped on their journey.

04:09.940 --> 04:11.060
﻿Stopped?

04:11.310 --> 04:12.730
﻿Apparently, three days ago...

04:12.860 --> 04:16.440
﻿...there was a cave-in at the St. Gotthard tunnel.

04:16.610 --> 04:19.280
﻿And, the trains going into Italy have all been stopped.

04:19.700 --> 04:22.700
﻿They said, it'll take another three days before they'll be up and running again.

04:24.120 --> 04:24.740
﻿There.

04:31.540 --> 04:34.380
﻿All right! We're going to Como, Italy!

04:34.480 --> 04:37.480
Vienna - Preminger Ducal Mansion

04:47.810 --> 04:49.390
﻿It's me, sir.

04:49.600 --> 04:50.390
﻿Come in.

04:52.480 --> 04:57.770
﻿Lady Colette and Count Waltmüller, have arrived.

04:58.360 --> 05:00.780
﻿With this, all the invited guests have arrived.

05:01.070 --> 05:01.990
﻿I see.

05:02.410 --> 05:05.910
﻿Also, you have a telegram from the detectives in Paris.

05:07.160 --> 05:09.490
﻿I will come to greet my guests after I've read this.

05:09.500 --> 05:11.410
﻿Yes, sir.

05:15.500 --> 05:18.550
﻿"Searched Paris after receiving information of her presence there..."

05:18.550 --> 05:21.300
﻿"But she seems to have left Paris already."

05:22.880 --> 05:24.090
﻿Useless fools!

05:27.390 --> 05:29.140
﻿Father? It's Colette.

05:29.430 --> 05:31.560
﻿Ohhh! Colette! Come on in.

05:32.600 --> 05:33.640
﻿Father...

05:34.650 --> 05:35.810
﻿Colette.

05:41.280 --> 05:44.570
﻿Father, happy birthday.

05:44.950 --> 05:46.070
﻿Thank you.

05:46.950 --> 05:48.240
﻿These are beautiful roses.

05:49.120 --> 05:50.580
﻿It has been a long time...

05:50.830 --> 05:52.160
﻿...your grace.

05:52.620 --> 05:56.000
﻿Thank you very much for your invitation.

05:56.460 --> 05:59.960
I know you are busy. Thank you for coming.

05:59.960 --> 06:01.460
﻿Count Waltmüller.

06:01.710 --> 06:05.680
﻿The guests have all arrived, shall we go down to meet them?

06:05.860 --> 06:06.530
Yes.

06:22.690 --> 06:26.700
﻿Happy birthday, your grace.

06:27.030 --> 06:29.160
﻿Thank you, Viscount Wellington.

06:29.780 --> 06:32.490
﻿I do not know if this will be to your liking, but...

06:32.580 --> 06:35.910
I have brought some wine that was made at our vineyard.

06:36.420 --> 06:37.370
﻿Thank you.

06:38.880 --> 06:40.420
﻿At the pheasant hunt this afternoon...

06:40.590 --> 06:43.250
﻿...let us see who will shoot the most birds.

06:43.260 --> 06:44.090
﻿Yes, indeed.

06:44.090 --> 06:45.590
﻿I will be looking forward to it.

06:49.680 --> 06:50.930
﻿Herman.

06:51.640 --> 06:52.720
﻿Father...

06:52.970 --> 06:55.060
H﻿appy birthday.

06:55.730 --> 06:57.690
﻿I do not remember inviting you!

06:57.900 --> 06:58.600
﻿Go home!

06:59.520 --> 07:00.480
﻿Father...!

07:00.610 --> 07:02.270
﻿I invited Herman.

07:02.270 --> 07:04.690
﻿Colette... What's the meaning of this?

07:05.150 --> 07:08.450
﻿Since Herman's wedding, you haven't seen him, have you...

07:08.780 --> 07:10.660
﻿If he was going to make up with you...

07:10.660 --> 07:13.120
﻿...I thought this would be a good opportunity.

07:13.870 --> 07:15.250
﻿That was unnecessary!

07:15.450 --> 07:16.160
﻿Your grace...

07:16.160 --> 07:18.370
﻿It was my fault as well.

07:18.750 --> 07:20.500
﻿Please do not blame Colette.

07:21.460 --> 07:23.000
I ﻿no longer care. Do as you like.

07:23.710 --> 07:25.420
﻿Thank you, father.

07:27.010 --> 07:29.380
﻿Hilda, thank you for coming.

07:29.390 --> 07:31.180
﻿For all your efforts...

07:31.180 --> 07:33.680
﻿...I really want to thank you, Lady Colette.

07:34.310 --> 07:36.560
﻿It has been a while, Aunt Colette.

07:37.100 --> 07:39.480
﻿Oscar! You've gotten so big!

07:39.980 --> 07:42.940
﻿Aunt Colette? you become more beautiful every time I see you.

07:47.240 --> 07:50.360
﻿What a surprise... you've turned into a real gentleman.

07:50.820 --> 07:51.530
﻿Ah! No...

07:51.530 --> 07:53.370
﻿Not at all.

07:57.120 --> 07:58.620
﻿Damn my father!

08:18.730 --> 08:19.390
﻿Huh?

08:23.360 --> 08:25.480
﻿Hey!!! What happened?

08:25.900 --> 08:27.360
I﻿'ll tell you what's happened!

08:27.360 --> 08:30.900
﻿We get here and he starts asking for double the fare!

08:31.240 --> 08:34.780
﻿When there's a storm, I have to risk my life to go over this pass!

08:35.030 --> 08:37.490
﻿It's not worth it for the regular fare.

08:38.040 --> 08:42.670
﻿W-When we got on at Andermatt, you didn't say a word of this!

08:42.670 --> 08:44.290
﻿If you don't want to pay, it's your choice!

08:44.460 --> 08:46.590
﻿I'll just go home.

08:46.590 --> 08:47.800
﻿You can't do that!

08:47.800 --> 08:49.760
By ﻿noon tomorrow, I have to...

08:50.050 --> 08:51.930
﻿...be in Locarno!

08:52.930 --> 08:56.760
﻿In that case, why don't we let them ride with us, Master?

08:57.720 --> 09:01.230
﻿Locarno in Italy is on the way to Como.

09:01.980 --> 09:04.150
﻿We all need help sometimes, right?

09:05.980 --> 09:06.900
You're right!

09:07.400 --> 09:09.610
﻿Everyone, you can ride with us if you like!

09:09.820 --> 09:13.570
﻿My car is much safer than that broken-down old carriage.

09:13.990 --> 09:15.410
﻿Is it really all right?

09:15.410 --> 09:16.140
Yeah!

09:16.450 --> 09:19.200
﻿I'll let you ride in my car, so hurry and get your luggage!

09:19.830 --> 09:20.700
﻿Oh, thank you! Thank you!

09:23.170 --> 09:24.080
﻿No thanks necessary!

09:36.390 --> 09:37.700
﻿Good boy!

09:37.700 --> 09:38.410
Nice shot!

09:38.890 --> 09:40.350
﻿Next, shall be my turn!

09:55.660 --> 09:57.160
﻿Herman!

09:57.910 --> 10:00.700
﻿Duke, please forgive my father's rudeness.

10:01.620 --> 10:03.330
﻿I will talk to him about this.

10:09.630 --> 10:11.630
﻿He seems to be a very fine young man.

10:12.050 --> 10:15.430
﻿It is a shame that he is not related to the Preminger family by blood.

10:16.890 --> 10:18.050
﻿Let us move on to another spot.

10:18.260 --> 10:18.890
﻿Yes, sir.

10:33.110 --> 10:34.820
﻿Master, do you need any help?

10:35.110 --> 10:37.410
﻿Nothing I can't handle myself.

10:37.410 --> 10:38.240
﻿Okay!

10:44.910 --> 10:46.210
﻿Why are we stopping?

10:49.840 --> 10:51.880
﻿Hey, hey, not now, please...

10:53.090 --> 10:54.590
﻿What's the matter, Master?

10:54.590 --> 10:56.550
﻿The engine won't run...

11:42.470 --> 11:43.470
﻿Master?

11:48.520 --> 11:49.730
﻿How is it?

11:49.940 --> 11:52.440
﻿Nothing seems to be broken...

11:52.980 --> 11:54.440
﻿But, it won't move.

11:54.570 --> 11:56.530
﻿Georg, what should we do?

11:56.900 --> 11:58.570
﻿The rain and wind is too strong...

11:59.110 --> 12:02.410
﻿The only thing to do is to wait for the storm to pass.

12:02.410 --> 12:03.740
﻿How can that be! We can't!

12:04.160 --> 12:06.540
﻿If we don't go over this pass tonight...

12:06.540 --> 12:08.960
﻿...we won't make it to Locarno by noon tomorrow!

12:09.040 --> 12:12.830
﻿Ahhhh, please, check again and make it move!

12:13.000 --> 12:15.040
﻿Uh... Even if you say so...

12:15.340 --> 12:17.510
﻿If I this was going to happen, I wish I had paid the money...

12:17.670 --> 12:19.880
﻿...and gotten on that carriage!

12:19.880 --> 12:21.840
﻿It's your fault for butting in!

12:22.260 --> 12:23.930
﻿How can you say that!

12:23.930 --> 12:26.060
﻿We gave you a ride out of kindness!

12:26.640 --> 12:29.060
﻿And, I'm saying,it wasn't your business!

12:29.060 --> 12:29.980
﻿What did you say...!

12:29.980 --> 12:30.940
﻿Kennosuke..

12:35.550 --> 12:41.050
Shizukeki mori no ue

12:35.550 --> 12:41.050
Above a quiet forest...

12:41.220 --> 12:46.560
Kagayakeru hoshi hitotsu

12:41.220 --> 12:46.560
A single shining star,

12:46.760 --> 12:52.100
Ai no uta kanaderu

12:46.760 --> 12:52.100
sings a song of love...

12:52.270 --> 12:57.900
Makiba no kaze yasashiku

12:52.270 --> 12:57.900
The wind blows gently in the pasture.

12:58.280 --> 13:03.200
Kotori mo koyagi mo

12:58.280 --> 13:03.200
All the little birds and the young kids,

13:03.360 --> 13:08.490
Haha ni idakare

13:03.360 --> 13:08.490
are held in their mother's embrace.

13:08.910 --> 13:14.420
Yume mite asobu no wa

13:08.910 --> 13:14.420
The place where we play in our dreams,

13:14.420 --> 13:22.800
Hana hiraku kaguwashiki niwa

13:14.420 --> 13:22.800
is a fragrant garden where the flowers bloom

13:25.800 --> 13:31.560
Sugiyuku kyou no hi no

13:25.800 --> 13:31.560
Today's sun is passing us by...

13:31.560 --> 13:37.020
Hohoemi o te no hira ni

13:31.560 --> 13:37.020
But, its smiles I will hold in my hand.

13:37.150 --> 13:42.570
Oyasumi, oyasumi

13:37.150 --> 13:42.570
I say good night, I say good night...

13:42.570 --> 13:46.030
Ko no te ni

13:42.570 --> 13:46.030
To this hand...

13:46.320 --> 13:50.830
Itoshii go yo

13:46.320 --> 13:50.830
My dear child...

13:59.150 --> 14:01.280
﻿Now, let's have a meal, shall we?

14:01.280 --> 14:02.780
﻿I'll help, too.

14:02.780 --> 14:04.400
﻿Well, thank you.

14:18.290 --> 14:21.090
﻿You should have gone pheasant hunting with us, Count.

14:21.170 --> 14:23.840
﻿I shot six birds.

14:24.170 --> 14:27.010
﻿Since I was a child, I've never been good at hunting.

14:27.090 --> 14:29.970
﻿That is pathetic, what with being a man and all.

14:32.270 --> 14:33.270
﻿Father?

14:33.270 --> 14:35.180
﻿I have to write a letter, so excuse me.

14:42.440 --> 14:44.990
﻿This is all we have, I'm sorry.

14:45.280 --> 14:49.410
﻿Not at all! We didn't expect to have any dinner.

14:49.410 --> 14:52.200
﻿Yes. This wine is delicious.

14:52.330 --> 14:54.750
﻿We stocked up on it in that last town.

14:54.750 --> 14:57.710
﻿We have more, so go ahead and drink!

14:58.920 --> 15:02.750
﻿Somehow, I feel cheated since we can't drink.

15:04.880 --> 15:08.840
﻿Hey, why are you in such a hurry to reach Locarno?

15:10.720 --> 15:14.100
﻿We want to attend a wedding there, tomorrow.

15:14.350 --> 15:15.640
﻿A wedding?

15:15.640 --> 15:18.060
﻿It's for the youngest of my six children...

15:18.270 --> 15:22.020
﻿We were poor, so we gave her up for adoption.

15:22.190 --> 15:25.320
﻿We thought she hated us, but instead she sent us money to come,

15:25.320 --> 15:27.360
﻿and asked us to be at the wedding...

15:27.360 --> 15:29.820
﻿Then you have to go for sure!

15:31.450 --> 15:33.910
﻿I'm going to see my family.

15:34.120 --> 15:36.120
﻿When I went to Switzerland for work...

15:36.120 --> 15:38.460
﻿I got in a fight over something stupid...

15:38.460 --> 15:41.880
﻿I was in jail for two years, and I just got out.

15:43.670 --> 15:46.590
﻿Well, everyone has their own reasons.

15:46.840 --> 15:49.380
﻿So, did you send word to your family?

15:50.640 --> 15:51.890
﻿I sent a telegram.

15:52.050 --> 15:53.390
﻿I said, I'll be home tomorrow.

15:54.180 --> 15:59.100
﻿Even though... I have no idea... whether or not my wife and child want me back...

15:59.940 --> 16:01.730
﻿They're waiting for you, for sure!

16:03.610 --> 16:04.520
﻿Little lady...

16:05.820 --> 16:06.690
﻿Thank you!

16:07.570 --> 16:10.780
﻿In that case, we won't make it on time, if we wait out the storm!

16:11.030 --> 16:14.950
﻿Okay! Everyone, it's a little dangerous, but let's cross that border!

16:15.200 --> 16:16.870
﻿Let's do it!!!

16:36.350 --> 16:37.260
Who is it??

16:37.270 --> 16:38.930
It is I. I'm coming in.

16:39.940 --> 16:43.100
﻿Because, you, the guest of honour is not there, everyone is quiet.

16:43.860 --> 16:46.650
﻿All except for Herman, am I right?

16:47.860 --> 16:48.900
﻿Father...

16:49.240 --> 16:51.990
﻿You have no intention in forgiving Herman, do you?

16:53.530 --> 16:54.700
﻿Of course, not.

16:55.030 --> 16:56.990
﻿Taking advantage of his position as the eldest son of the Preminger family,

16:56.990 --> 16:58.040
﻿he lived a life of complete dissipation.

16:58.870 --> 17:00.450
﻿In the end, he...

17:00.540 --> 17:03.000
﻿...sold a part of my lands without my knowledge...

17:03.170 --> 17:06.250
﻿...and put the money into a worthless business and lost everything!

17:06.250 --> 17:07.920
﻿That is true, but...

17:09.010 --> 17:12.090
﻿Now that I have married into the Waltmüller family...

17:12.260 --> 17:14.930
﻿...the only heir to the Dukedom is Herman.

17:15.260 --> 17:16.600
﻿But, Na-...

17:17.310 --> 17:17.810
﻿What?

17:17.810 --> 17:19.470
﻿Uh, Humph... nothing.

17:20.480 --> 17:22.350
﻿I will come after I have finished writing this letter.

17:22.850 --> 17:24.060
﻿I understand.

17:24.310 --> 17:28.020
﻿I would like to be your partner for the dance, father.

17:28.360 --> 17:29.280
﻿Yes.

17:37.280 --> 17:40.240
﻿To Colette, who believes that her daughter died...

17:40.500 --> 17:42.410
﻿I cannot speak about Nadja.

17:57.550 --> 17:59.760
﻿The road is getting narrower.

18:00.890 --> 18:03.810
﻿Kennosuke, please go a little to the right!

18:03.810 --> 18:04.520
﻿Yeah!

18:08.230 --> 18:09.610
﻿Nadja!

18:09.860 --> 18:10.770
﻿What's the matter?!

18:10.780 --> 18:12.440
﻿Nadja went over the cliff!

18:13.650 --> 18:15.820
﻿Kennosuke, get the lamp, quickly!

18:16.530 --> 18:17.700
﻿Are you okay?

18:18.580 --> 18:20.910
﻿I'm here! Help me!

18:20.890 --> 18:22.450
﻿Nadja!

18:23.160 --> 18:25.410
﻿I'll go. Everyone pull.

18:30.960 --> 18:32.670
﻿I'm coming, Nadja!

18:33.090 --> 18:35.590
﻿Master, please come quickly!!!

18:35.840 --> 18:37.430
﻿Don't let go!

18:37.640 --> 18:40.510
﻿If you let go, you're fired from the Dandelion Troupe!

18:41.350 --> 18:44.600
﻿I hear you, but I'm running out of strength...

18:49.270 --> 18:51.020
﻿That was a narrow escape!

18:51.820 --> 18:53.480
﻿M-Master...

18:56.530 --> 18:57.200
﻿...Nadja...

18:57.820 --> 18:58.860
﻿...Nadja, wake up...

18:59.070 --> 19:00.660
﻿Hey! Nadja!

19:02.120 --> 19:04.200
﻿I'm... okay?

19:04.330 --> 19:05.580
﻿Thank goodness!

19:05.580 --> 19:07.210
﻿Don't make me worry like that!

19:08.790 --> 19:10.330
﻿Rita, please don't cry.

19:10.380 --> 19:11.960
﻿I'm fine.

19:12.710 --> 19:14.460
﻿Little lady, I'm sorry.

19:14.460 --> 19:16.670
﻿For our selfish reasons, you almost...

19:16.880 --> 19:18.930
﻿Let's wait here until morning.

19:19.050 --> 19:20.510
﻿What are you saying!

19:20.600 --> 19:22.970
﻿Your daughter and your family are waiting for you!

19:23.270 --> 19:26.060
﻿No matter what, let's get to Locarno by noon tomorrow!

19:26.180 --> 19:27.430
﻿Hey, Nadja...!

19:27.810 --> 19:30.190
﻿Now, everybody, push! Push!

19:30.610 --> 19:32.730
﻿All right! It's just a little more to the top!

19:32.860 --> 19:34.280
﻿Everyone, let's do it!

19:34.320 --> 19:35.570
﻿Yeah!!!

19:40.970 --> 19:44.520
